"""
Forecast Yield Predictability
=============================
Per-region (index_type, window) selected on OBSERVED temperatures over
2000-2015. Forecast engines are evaluated out-of-sample on 2016-2024.

  Calibration  : 2000-2015  (observed T + yield)
  Holdout      : 2016-2024  (9 years × 9 models)

  Stage 1 — Pre-OOS, on observed data only:
    * Detrend yield over years ≤ 2015 (linear OLS in year).
    * Search 3 index types × 15 contiguous March-July month-block windows
      = 45 candidates. Pick the (itype, window) whose observed accumulated
      index correlates most strongly (max |Pearson r|) with detrended yield.
    * Fit yield form (linear / quadratic-only / linear+quadratic) by BIC
      with a parsimony tie-break on the chosen (itype, window).
    Forecast engines play no role in selection.

  Stage 2 — Holdout, per forecast engine:
    For each (model, region, year) in 2017-2024, accumulate the model's
    daily point forecasts (bk_forecasts.csv) through the frozen
    (itype, window) to give I_hat, plug into the frozen form -> Y_hat.
    Compare to detrended actual yield. Report RMSE / MAE / ME / MAPE /
    RMSE % R̄ on revenue (EUR/ha) at 160 EUR/t wheat price.

Outputs (in 99_Thesis Graphs/03_Results/04_Hedging Effectiveness/):
  P01_yield_model_per_region_BIC.png     selection table (structural ceiling)
  P02_forecast_accuracy_per_model.png    aggregate per-model accuracy
  P03_forecast_rmse_matrix.png           model × region RMSE matrix
  P04_revenue_predictions_over_years.png actual vs predicted revenue per region
  P06_forecast_rmse_matrix_year.png      model × year RMSE matrix
"""

